  <div class="eyebrow" style="color:var(--worm)">Diagram 2 · Engine Close-Up — Worm Spine Detail</div>
  <h2 class="section-title">High-Lead Worm Spine · Helical Gear Mesh · Cylinder Shaft Detail</h2>
  <p class="section-lead">
    The core innovation of the Miasma Decker 9000 engine. Three cylinder shafts running left to right each carry a precision helical gear at their midpoint.
    Each helical gear meshes into one of three dedicated high-lead worm sections on the central driveshaft running front to back.
    The steep lead angle of the worm thread allows the helical gears to back-drive the worm spine — converting left-right cylinder rotation into front-back driveshaft rotation.
    All three gear-worm pairs are clean separated, oil bathed, and independently serviceable.
  </p>

