      <div class="badge" style="color:var(--ctrl);border-color:var(--ctrl)">Bonus Discovery</div>
      <h3>Torque Vectoring via Independent Pipes</h3>
      <p>Two independent steam pipes with individual PCW throttle valves means each side of the engine can receive different steam pressure. Left side gets more steam = left cylinders produce more torque. This is essentially steam-powered torque vectoring — a differential-like steering assist built into the engine architecture at no extra cost.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
